; Asuka, Black Hole's intelligence chief: "Umbra Protocol" (remix A), a cold, sinister theme in A harmonic minor with the tritone (Eb) and the flat second (Bb) pulling against the tonic.
; Original composition for tangoAW2. Low horns speak a slow, chromatically falling phrase over a timpani heartbeat; the clock of the first theme is kept but muted and low, its last tick of every bar
; a tritone; the strings hold the flat second (Bb against the A below); a muted trumpet answers in the second section, the bass walks down the chromatic scale in the last, and a crash stings the loop shut.
;
; Form: two bars of heartbeat and clock, then the loop: the horns (A), the trumpet's answer (B), the horns with the eerie high flute (A2) and the descent (C). 32 bars at 100 beats a minute: about 77 s.
song asuka
tempo 100
meter 4/4
reverb 173
priority 0

inst horns   = A.111 shift=-12      ; low brass, the voice of the file
inst pluck   = A.117 shift=0        ; the clock, muted
inst strings = A.48                 ; the cluster
inst bass    = A.36  shift=24       ; pick bass
inst trumpet = A.56  shift=-12      ; muted by its velocity
inst kit     = A.120
inst timp    = A.47  shift=24       ; the heartbeat
inst flute   = A.77  shift=-12      ; the eerie high voice

hit kick=36 rim=37 snare=40 hat=44 ohat=46 tom1=45 tom2=48 tom3=50 crash=49

track 1 inst=horns   vol=84 pan=-6  vel=110 gate=92 gain=1.15
track 2 inst=pluck   vol=52 pan=18  vel=76  gate=50 gain=2.4
track 3 inst=strings vol=48 pan=-22 vel=84  gate=100 gain=1.6
track 4 inst=bass    vol=86 pan=0   vel=114 gate=92 gain=0.85
track 5 inst=trumpet vol=64 pan=14  vel=96  gate=60 gain=1.9
track 6 inst=kit     vol=62 pan=0   vel=100 gate=100 gain=1.2
track 7 inst=timp    vol=80 pan=0   vel=118 gate=95 gain=0.8
track 8 inst=flute   vol=56 pan=24  vel=84  gate=90 gain=1.2

; ---- the horns: Am Am Bb E | Am F Eb E (the Eb is the tritone) ----
def thA:
  | A3/2. Bb3/4 |
  | A3/4. G#3/8 A3/4 E3/4 |
  | D4/2. C#4/4 |
  | C4/4 B3/4 G#3/2 |
  | A3/4. A3/8 C4/4 E4/4 |
  | F4/2. E4/4 |
  | Eb4/4. D4/8 Eb4/4 A3/4 |
  | E4/4. D#4/8 D4/4 B3/4 |
end
; ---- the trumpet's answer, high and muted: Dm Dm Bb E | Dm Bb E E ----
def thB:
  | r/4 A4/4 D5/2 |
  | C5/4. Bb4/8 A4/2 |
  | D5/4 Bb4/4 F4/2 |
  | G#4/4 B4/4 E5/2 |
  | r/4 A4/4 D5/2 |
  | F5/4. E5/8 D5/4 Bb4/4 |
  | B4/4 G#4/4 E4/4 B4/4 |
  | Bb4/2 A4/2 |
end
; ---- the descent: Am G F E | Eb D C# E ----
def thC:
  | A3/4 C4/4 E4/2 |
  | G3/4 B3/4 D4/2 |
  | F3/4 A3/4 C4/2 |
  | E3/4 G#3/4 B3/2 |
  | Eb4/4. D4/8 Eb4/4 Bb3/4 |
  | D4/4. C4/8 D4/4 A3/4 |
  | C#4/4. B3/8 C#4/4 G#3/4 |
  | E4/1 |
end
; ---- the eerie flute, high, a long line a compound fifth above the horns ----
def flA:
  | E5/1 |
  | Eb5/2 D5/2 |
  | F5/1 |
  | B4/2 G#4/2 |
  | C6/1 |
  | A5/2 Bb5/2 |
  | G5/2 Eb5/2 |
  | E5/1 |
end
; ---- the clock (Am written): a tick every eighth, the last one the tritone ----
def ost:
  | A3/8 E4/8 A3/8 E4/8 A3/8 E4/8 A3/8 Eb4/8 |
end
; ---- the bass (A written) ----
def bs:
  | A1/4 r/8 A1/8 A1/4 r/4 |
end
def bsw:
  | A1/4 A1/4 A1/4 A1/4 |
end
; ---- the heartbeat (A written) ----
def hb:
  | A1/8 A1/8 r/4 A1/8 A1/8 r/4 |
end
; ---- the strings: the flat second above A, and in the last section the tritone ----
def clu:
  | Bb3/1 |
end
def tri:
  | Eb4/1 |
end
; ---- drums ----
def kd:
  | r/2 tom1/4 r/4 |
end
def kdr:
  | r/2 tom1/4 tom2/8 tom3/8 |
end
def kdc:
  | kick/4 r/4 snare/4 r/4 |
end
def kde:
  | kick/4 snare/8 snare/8 snare/8 snare/8 snare/8 snare/8 |
end

section intro bars=2
  7: @hb @hb
  2: {vol 40>60/192} @ost @ost
end

section A bars=8
  1: {vol 84} @thA
  2: @ost @ost @ost+1 @ost+7 @ost @ost-4 @ost+6 @ost+7
  3: {vol 46} @clu @clu @clu+1 @clu+7 @clu @clu-4 @clu+6 @clu+7
  4: {vol 86} @bs @bs @bs+1 @bs+7 @bs @bs-4 @bs+6 @bs+7
  7: @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb
  6: {vol 56} @kd @kd @kd @kd @kd @kd @kd @kdr
end

section B bars=8
  5: {vol 66} @thB
  2: @ost+5 @ost+5 @ost+1 @ost+7 @ost+5 @ost+1 @ost+7 @ost+7
  3: {vol 50} @clu+5 @clu+5 @clu+1 @clu+7 @clu+5 @clu+1 @clu+7 @clu+7
  4: {vol 86} @bs+5 @bs+5 @bs+1 @bs+7 @bs+5 @bs+1 @bs+7 @bs+7
  7: @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb
  6: {vol 60} @kd @kd @kd @kd @kd @kd @kd @kdr
end

section A2 bars=8
  1: {vol 84} @thA
  8: @flA
  2: @ost @ost @ost+1 @ost+7 @ost @ost-4 @ost+6 @ost+7
  4: {vol 88} @bsw @bsw @bsw+1 @bsw+7 @bsw @bsw-4 @bsw+6 @bsw+7
  7: @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb
  6: {vol 64} @kd @kd @kd @kd @kd @kdc @kdc @kdr
end

section C bars=8
  1: {vol 90} @thC
  2: @ost @ost-2 @ost-4 @ost-5 @ost+6 @ost+5 @ost+4 @ost+7
  3: {vol 52} @tri @tri-2 @tri-4 @tri-5 @tri+6 @tri+5 @tri+4 @tri+7
  4: {vol 90} @bsw @bsw-2 @bsw-4 @bsw-5 @bsw+6 @bsw+5 @bsw+4 @bsw+7
  7: @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb @hb
  6: {vol 66} @kdc @kdc @kdc @kdc @kdc @kdc @kdc @kde
end

form intro loop A B A2 C
